---
import DocsLayout from '../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';

const providers = [
  { name: 'OpenCode Zen', access: 'Free model routes', setup: 'No key' },
  { name: 'Kilo Gateway', access: 'Free model routes', setup: 'No key' },
  { name: 'OI VSCode Server', access: 'Community endpoint', setup: 'No key' },
  { name: 'Ollama', access: 'Models installed locally', setup: 'Run Ollama' },
  { name: 'OpenRouter', access: 'Free models and free router', setup: 'ghost login openrouter' },
  { name: 'Groq', access: 'Free developer quota', setup: 'ghost login groq' },
  { name: 'Google AI', access: 'Models with a free API tier', setup: 'ghost login googleai' },
  { name: 'Cloudflare Workers AI', access: 'Daily free allocation', setup: 'Set CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID, then ghost login cloudflare' },
  { name: 'Cohere', access: 'Trial key quota', setup: 'ghost login cohere' },
  { name: 'NVIDIA NIM', access: 'Developer API access', setup: 'ghost login nvidia-nim' },
  { name: 'AMD Radeon Cloud', access: 'Free Token Factory quota', setup: 'ghost login amd-radeon' },
  { name: 'Aion Labs', access: 'Free account quota', setup: 'ghost login aion' },
  { name: 'Hugging Face', access: 'Monthly account credits', setup: 'ghost login huggingface' },
  { name: 'LLM7', access: 'Free daily token quota', setup: 'ghost login llm7' },
  { name: 'OpenTyphoon', access: 'Free research API', setup: 'ghost login typhoon' },
  { name: 'Nous Portal', access: 'Models with zero-price routes', setup: 'ghost login nous-portal' },
  { name: 'Cerebras', access: 'One-time promotional credit', setup: 'ghost login cerebras' },
];
---

<DocsLayout title="Providers & Models" description="Live model catalogs and provider setup.">
  <p>
    Ghost refreshes model lists from provider APIs and keeps a local cache for offline starts.
    Use <code>ghost free</code> to see what is available to your configured accounts.
  </p>

  <h2>Provider access</h2>
  <p>Free access can mean a zero-price model, a usage quota, or a limited credit balance. Check each provider's limits and terms.</p>
  <table class="docs-table">
    <thead><tr><th>Provider</th><th>Free access</th><th>Setup</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      {providers.map((provider) => (
        <tr><td>{provider.name}</td><td>{provider.access}</td><td><code>{provider.setup}</code></td></tr>
      ))}
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>Add a provider key</h2>
  <p>Run <code>ghost login</code> with the provider ID. Ghost prompts for the key without echoing it and saves it in your global config.</p>
  <pre class="block"><code>ghost login openrouter
ghost login nvidia-nim
ghost free</code></pre>
  <p>Cloudflare also needs the account ID in <code>CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID</code>. Set it in the environment before launching Ghost.</p>
  <p>See the <a href="https://github.com/swadhinbiswas/Ghost/blob/main/docs/free-model-providers.md">provider guide</a> for current limits, terms, and source links.</p>

  <div class="callout warn">
    Model lists, free quotas, and account eligibility change. Some providers may switch to paid use after a quota or credit runs out. Review the provider's current terms before use.
  </div>
</DocsLayout>
